digest with  acidic digestive enzymes whereas cups  requires an alkaline environment with  alkaline enzymes your typical diet pairs  meat and starch in one meal for example  you might enjoy a piece of steak  together with potatoes or  chicken with rice protein and cups have  opposite digestive requirements and  eating them together causes your body to  release both acid and alkaline solutions  the acid and alkaline solutions will  neutralize each other which can slow  digestion and cause post meal  sluggishness or bloating this is because  your body is using more energy digesting  than needed hence understanding food  combining principles can help support  the health of your entire gut here are  five really simple principles first do  not combine protein with starch in a  meal as you know now in order to be  digested protein needs an acidic  environment which is why it is  considered a bad combination to eat  protein with starch in a meal instead  consume protein with non-starchy  vegetables such as leafy greens broccoli  cauliflower  carrots cabbage cucumber celery bell  peppers onions and more these vegetables  are rich in their own enzymes hence they  don't need an alkaline environment for  digestion and because of that they won't  interfere with the acidic environment  required by protein this principle also  applies to plant proteins such as beans  and legumes so here's what a good  combination would look like  while salmon with broccoli and carrots  chicken with kale and cauliflower  tofu with bell peppers onions and celery  second pear starch with healthy fats and  non-starchy vegetables starches such as  brown rice quinoa barley along with  starchy vegetables such as sweet potato  corn and squash need an alkaline  environment for digestion so this is  what a good food combination would look  like  baked potato with avocado and stir-fried  vegetables quinoa and pumpkin with nuts  and seeds and leafy greens and cherry  tomatoes brown rice and stir-fried  vegetables cooked with coconut oil by  now you should know that leafy greens  and non-starchy vegetables go well with  everything they contain their own  digestive enzymes hence can be paired  with any food without causing a traffic  jam in your gi tract if you're totally  confused with the food combining rules  to keep it simple simply choose a single  macronutrient whether it's protein  starch or healthy fats with leafy greens  or non-starchy vegetables it is as easy  as that the next principle eat fruits  alone fruit is a simple sugar that  digests very rapidly in roughly 20 to 30  minutes whereas protein for example can  take between three to four hours to  digest now if you combine fruits and  protein in a single meal it can create  chaos in your gi tract because of the  different time needed for the food to be  digested that is why it is also best to  avoid eating fruits right after meals  since fruits digest faster than any  other food they are best to be eaten  alone so that they do not have the  chance to ferment as i've mentioned  earlier fermentation in your gi tract  will make you feel bloated and gassy so  it is best to consume fruits alone the  final important guideline is to avoid  drinking water together with your meals  water can dilute your digestive fluids  which can slow down digestion now before  knowing this i used to drink lots of  water with my meals and would feel  extremely bloated and even experience  stomach pain if you really need to have  small sips of water with your meals and  try to drink most of your water away  from your meals you can also aid your  digestion by drinking lemon water  roughly 20 to 30 minutes before a meal  lemon contains ascorbic acid which can  help stimulate digestion i drink lemon  water on an empty stomach first thing in  the morning now there really isn't  enough scientific research to back the  food combining principles but the reason  why i'm sharing this with you is because  it has worked for me i'm someone who 